ts_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-05T11:07:17Z","updated_at":"2026-06-05T11:07:17Z","body":"Sorry for the flood of comments but I think this bug is maybe a duplicate of https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/98764, which for some reason I simply didnt find on my initial search when trying to solve this bug","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4630872689/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4661430735","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120029#issuecomment-4661430735","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120029","id":4661430735,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABFdfJzw","user":{"login":"GiacomoPope","id":44242839,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0MjQyODM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44242839?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope","html_url":"https://github.com/GiacomoPope","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/GiacomoPope/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-09T15:39:18Z","updated_at":"2026-06-09T15:55:16Z","body":"If people are interested I have a work around.\n\n---\n\nThe idea is to have a separate viewport to hold the particles. My workflow has:\n\n1. A viewport with full resolution for HD textures\n2. A sub viewport scaled 4x with 2D transform pixel snapping to true, this is where the whole game is, called `SubViewport`\n3. A second sub viewport without 2D transform pixel snapping, called `ShadowSubViewport`\n\nIn `ShadowSubViewport` I have a single `Node2D` which I call `ShadowPlayer`. The script for this node is simple:\n\n```gdscript\nclass_name PlayerShadow\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready() -> void:\n    GameManager.register_shadow(self)\n\nfunc _physics_process(_delta: float) -> void:\n    # Follow the player\n    global_position = GameManager.player.global_position\n\n    # Ensure the shadow viewport follows the main game viewport\n    var main_vp = GameManager.player.get_viewport()\n    get_viewport().canvas_transform = main_vp.canvas_transform\n```\n\nThen, the player, which is a child of `SubViewport` has the following \"hack\":\n\n```gdscript\nfunc _send_particles_to_shadow() -> void:\n\tfor child in GameManager.shadow.get_children():\n\t\tchild.queue_free()\n\n\tfor child in particles.get_children():\n\t\tif not child is GPUParticles2D:\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\tparticles.remove_child(child)\n\t\tGameManager.shadow.add_child(child)\n``` \n\nThe idea here is that the player has all the particles and information but when the player is introduced into the tree we move every particle (held in a particles `Node2D` just for organisation) and reparent them to the Shadow\n\nNow, the particles move with the player, but in a sub viewport without the snapping, avoiding the jitter bug.\n ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4661430735/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]